{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>How your garments are hot</b> — the meaning is the days of summer, for most of the winds are from the left, because the sun is in the region of the left." "And most of the commentators said: <b>to be quiet</b> (lehashkit) — when it arrives, which is the opposite of quiet (sheket); and they said it is like 'a land of awe and quiet' [Esther 9:20?]. This is far-fetched, for one word to be interpreted by its opposite without a change in form, like shoresh and shoresh. And it would have been more correct for them to say: Can you become hot, were there not a south wind?!"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:53.961032008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}